  },
  "rules": {
    "oracle": "When this creature enters, draw two cards, then discard two cards. When you discard one or more nonland cards this way, tap up to that many target creatures and put a stun counter on each of them.\n{3}{U}{U}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Draw two cards.",
    "cr": [
      "603.12",
      "603.3d",
      "115.1",
      "601.2c",
      "122.1d",
      "608.2c"
    ],
    "actual": "The enters trigger draws two and discards two, but the reflexive \"When you discard one or more nonland cards this way\" trigger is Unimplemented (zone_change_reflexive_unbound_referent): no creature is ever tapped or stunned.",
    "expected": "If one or more of the discarded cards are nonland cards, a reflexive triggered ability triggers (CR 603.12). Its controller chooses up to N target creatures as it is put on the stack (CR 603.3d, 601.2c), where N is the number of nonland cards discarded this way (one or two), and on resolution taps them and puts a stun counter on each. Discarding two lands means no trigger. A stunned permanent stays tapped through its controller's next untap step, losing the counter instead (CR 122.1d). The graveyard ability is already right.",
    "diagnosis": "zone_change_reflexive.rs fails closed when the reflexive body both says \"target\" and contains an anaphor (\"each of them\" lowers to PutCounter target ParentTarget), on the theory that the anaphor might refer to an unbound referent from before the reflexive. Here \"them\" is the reflexive's own targets, the ordinary \"tap up to N target creatures and put a stun counter on each of them\" shape (Out Cold), so the guard over-rejects.",
    "suggested_fix": "In parser/oracle_effect/zone_change_reflexive.rs, before rejecting a reflexive body for an unbound referent, resolve anaphors against the body's own target phrase: when \"them\"/\"each of them\" follows \"target <noun>\" inside the same reflexive clause, it binds to those targets (ParentTarget within the body chain), so the body lowers like Out Cold's SetTapState(Creature, multi_target) -> PutCounter(stun, ParentTarget). For \"up to that many\", count only the cards matching the trigger's filter: multi_target { min: 0, max: FilteredTrackedSetSize { filter: nonland card, caused_by: Discarded } } (EventContextAmount, as used by Nyssa of Traken, would count all discarded cards), under condition And[WhenYouDo, ZoneChangedThisWay(nonland card)]. Narset of the Ancient Way, Three Dog, Galaxy News DJ and Vivien's Invocation hit the same guard.",
    "override_note": "The patch builds the reflexive from shapes 0.116.0 already runs: the gate And[WhenYouDo, ZoneChangedThisWay(nonland card)] with a multi_target slot count from Nyssa of Traken (\"When you sacrifice one or more artifacts this way, tap up to that many target creatures\"), the count of nonland cards discarded from Seasoned Pyromancer (FilteredTrackedSetSize, caused_by Discarded, which leaves out the drawn cards of the same draw-then-discard), and the tap-and-stun body from Out Cold. The reflexive goes on the stack after the discard with its targets chosen then (CR 603.12, 603.3d), from 0 up to the number of nonland cards discarded; with no nonland card discarded it doesn't trigger. Tests cover two, one and zero nonland discards, choosing fewer targets, and the stun counter at the next untap step (CR 122.1d)."
  },
